{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27625-need-a-little-help-with-my-campaign","id":27625,"title":"Need a little help with my campaign...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-10T17:09:47-08:00","id":27625,"title":"Need a little help with my campaign...","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> So I need a little help with my ongoing Mummy game.<br /> <br /> To give some perspective on the game: -<br /> <br /> Its a Changeling/Mummy crossover (we've been calling it Chummy) that's centered around the theme of <b>Identity</b> (as its the theme that crosses over between the two games most obviously). <br /> <br /> The games been running since April of this year and is at current about a third of the way through the &quot;second act&quot; (its got 3 acts in total, with act 1 being the largest). <br /> <br /> The setting is the City of York and the play-style was very &quot;slice of life&quot; (literally every day has been played through from April 9th to April 16th before IC events meant the group &quot;time-skipped&quot; to June 23rd and played until June 26th) with hidden truths. Some major &quot;behind the scenes&quot; manipulation is going on and due to both the PC Mummy's have been running into plots that their past selves kicked off centuries and decades ago. Likewise, the Changelings memories of her durance have been proven to be faulty a few times and simply absent in others. <br /> <br /> Recently the main player group (two high Memory Mummy's (they both have worked their way up to a rating of 7 from 3) and a Changeling) have gone off to do some &quot;memory&quot; hunting in places around the world they remember as important in past descents. They've visited Budapest, Istanbul (which they plan on returning too, as they have unfinished business there) and have just arrived in Rome. The tone of the game has also changed, taking on a more &quot;episodic&quot; feel (not my usual ST style) with &quot;downtimes&quot; of a couple of days as the group travels from city to city. <br /> <br /> I've got a lot of the plot I wanted to run for them sorted in Rome. However I wrote it all about 4 weeks ago (real life has gotten in the way of me running the session since then) and looking back on it I'm not warming to my own stuff so much. <br /> <br /> To give some perspective on the OC circumstances: -<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, the game-style has changed to one that is not typical style. However, while I'm trying to engage with it I don't find it inherently troublesome. Good to broaden play styles and all that. There are a number of contextual points that I feel bear some import on the campaigns continuation:<br /> <br /> 1) I usually run Campaigns for about a year to a year and a half, so running anything is massive commitment for me. <br /> <br /> 2) This particular Campaign has suffered from thematic issues between Mummy and Changeling and the choices I have made in my design of the metaphysics and metaplot of my world. This has led to group issues (the Changeling was getting carried around like a &quot;backpack&quot; for a while and was having trouble contributing). <br /> <br /> 3) I tried to ad-lib some stuff when it came to the Changeling part of the game (as I had not re-read the books for about a year when writing this campaign), two of my players are ST and rules ST for our local Changeling Live game. They picked up on my less then complete games mastery and slight unease with Changeling in general (I like the game, but I don't completely &quot;get it&quot; and have issue with the amount its content gets &quot;fanboyed&quot; into other gamelines sometimes) so I since have re-read the books. <br /> <br /> 4) I'm writing a new Vampire setting (using Blood and Smoke) for a local Vampire Live game which is going to be eating my time once that book is out. So I'm not likely to have so much time or Chummy at that point. <br /> <br /> 5) I have a habit of getting board about 9 months into my campaigns and get excited about Onyx Path new gamelines. I'm part of the Demon kickstarter and really like the look of the game, so I'll likely be reading the pdf soon. Not constructive to Chummy writing (I don't want to include Demons in my setting). <br /> <br /> 6) I'm currently working 2 jobs (which I was not when I started running this campaign) so I have even less time to write then I did (or would like to). <br /> <br /> So to finally get the point, with all the above being true and very general can you helpful, wonderful people here on the Onyx Path forums help me out? <br /> <br /> Basically, considering all the above, I'm very interested in peoples general thoughts for plot ideas for the campaign (Roman themed, working with the theme of Identity, cool possible points of crossover for Changeling and Mummy's etc). As I'm hoping a bit of a brain storm and discussion might spark something in my mind and get me over my current block. <br /> <br /> Thanks beforehand to everyone who takes the time to contribute to this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:20:04-08:00","id":27770,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's plot ideas you need?<br /> <br /> You'll like this thread, then:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\"> 1001 Mummy Story Hooks - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Reposting my old 1001 Mummy Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful. Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I created this thread on three separate fora. .) The first time a PC increases her Memory, she recalls that her Judge, back in Duat, warned her about </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:26:17-08:00","id":27963,"title":"","content":"You're in York? As in, UK York? 'cause I used to live there. Cool stuff. I have a ton on York-based Requiem/Blood and Smoke stuff you might like.<br /> <br /> I need more information on what's bringing the Lost and Arisen together and a loose idea of their local societies. You mention Roman - your Arisen were active in Eboracum, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:18:01-08:00","id":27986,"title":"","content":"Well you should give some spotlight to the Changeling soon, I would think.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Changeling's Keeper has been stealing people from all over the world, or at least from the contemporary nations of the ancient Roman empire. Perhaps It fancies itself as a Caesar-style Emperor, or it abducts those with imperial blood in them. As the Mummies travel over old Rome and re-discover their Memories, so the Changeling should be piecing together who their Keeper was, why It abducted him, and how it can prevent more abductions from occurring.<br /> <br /> What level of Sekhem are your Mummies at right now? The Descent chart is easy to calculate an estimate of how long the rest of their Descent will be. Plan your chronicle ending roughly around that time. The Descent is finite, and so, apparently, is your own time, energy, and interest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so it's a very good time-frame to use, and it's best to give your story a bang at the finish rather than a drawn out whimper.<br /> <br /> There's two goals here: for the Mummies, they're reclaiming their Memory; for the Changeling, it's re-integrating themselves into society and, at least one day, ending their Keeper. Will the Keeper die? Probably not, if your time is on a budget. The same goes for Mummies claiming Apotheosis. So keep the stakes on their scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:43:07-08:00","id":29099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27625-need-a-little-help-with-my-campaign?p=27963#post27963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're in York? As in, UK York? 'cause I used to live there. Cool stuff. I have a ton on York-based Requiem/Blood and Smoke stuff you might like.<br /> <br /> I need more information on what's bringing the Lost and Arisen together and a loose idea of their local societies. You mention Roman - your Arisen were active in Eboracum, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll very tempted to take you up on that Eremite when it comes to writing my Leeds based Vampire LARP in the next few months. <br /> <br /> As for what's giving the group a reason to hang out. The Changeling in question is the &quot;first purpose&quot; of one of the Mummy's. Her &quot;uncle&quot; (currently in the body of a 14 year old boy, long story, he's a reborn, its complicated) woke up his long time companion (one of the Mummy's) because he was sure something &quot;bad&quot; was going to happen/was happening to his favorite niece. Unfortunately. he was a few years late with his and she had already been taken to Arcadia and escaped back, done some travelling and ended up in York by &quot;fate&quot; basically. <br /> <br /> The second Mummy is a long time ally to the first, he's kinda sorta avoiding his &quot;first purpose&quot; (it involves perching his cult's family line) by doing a lot of the &quot;secondary purpose&quot; things he meant to help out with, including aiding the first Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:54:49-08:00","id":29107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27625-need-a-little-help-with-my-campaign?p=27963#post27963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well you should give some spotlight to the Changeling soon, I would think.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Changeling's Keeper has been stealing people from all over the world, or at least from the contemporary nations of the ancient Roman empire. Perhaps It fancies itself as a Caesar-style Emperor, or it abducts those with imperial blood in them. As the Mummies travel over old Rome and re-discover their Memories, so the Changeling should be piecing together who their Keeper was, why It abducted him, and how it can prevent more abductions from occurring.<br /> <br /> What level of Sekhem are your Mummies at right now? The Descent chart is easy to calculate an estimate of how long the rest of their Descent will be. Plan your chronicle ending roughly around that time. The Descent is finite, and so, apparently, is your own time, energy, and interest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so it's a very good time-frame to use, and it's best to give your story a bang at the finish rather than a drawn out whimper.<br /> <br /> There's two goals here: for the Mummies, they're reclaiming their Memory; for the Changeling, it's re-integrating themselves into society and, at least one day, ending their Keeper. Will the Keeper die? Probably not, if your time is on a budget. The same goes for Mummies claiming Apotheosis. So keep the stakes on their scale</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<br /> <br /> The Changelings Keeper his currently in-exile in the material world. She believes she's a 18 year old A-Level student who's been in a coma for two years. Basically, she lost a game (thanks to actions the player does not remember her character taking while still in Arcadia) and had to flee Arcadia. She's gone native. The Changeling is basically a loyalist, in that she does not actually hate or blame her Keeper for the most part (she lost a lot of herself in Arcadia, so she can't remember a lot of the terrible things that happened). Ironically one of the charities (read: Cults) that one of the Mummy PC's owns is currently helping the Changeling PC's keeper deal with the trauma of &quot;waking up&quot; from a a two year coma. <br /> <br /> The Mummy's are at Sekhem 4, very near dropping to Sekhem 3. However, the Sothic turn is literally just about to start in about a week in game. So they are going to get a reset before they run dry, likely when they are on Sekhem 2 or 1 even. <br /> <br /> The overarching framework is that the Mummy's want to remember the whole truth of the long list of schemes they seem to have set up and WHY they did such crazy planning in the past. The Changeling just wants to make sure her &quot;friends&quot; (the Mummy's) are OK and that things don't spiral to all hell for the people she cares about. Yes there is a lot of unresolved stuff with the Keeper that could go in a lot of different directions, but that's slowly bubbling up in the background. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, while both Mummy's are seeking high Memory, its purely for selfish or &quot;immediate&quot; reasons. Neither are sold on the idea of Apotheosis or the Heretics claims. Despite one of them having had at least some dealings with the Heretic in the past. <br /> <br /> The idea of the Keeper claiming people is in the background. Another gentry is posing as a &quot;dark mysterious stranger&quot; traveling from Freehold to Freehold across Europe and doing all sorts of weird stuff. In Budapest he convinced the Day Court Monarch to &quot;become&quot; his kingdom using &quot;bones&quot; of a &quot;dead god&quot; buried under the city. I was thinking of him having payed a visit to Rome as well and having done something odd to the Freehold there as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T20:17:35-08:00","id":29681,"title":"","content":"well, ive got a couple of ideas to consider. the first one involves an area that is an overlap between the two games--Fate. Mummies interact with fate in various ways, and at the very least believe in it. changeling, however, is directly intwined into fate. to bring in more changeling esque elements, plllay up on that. for example, maybe one of the mummies begins to realize that Fate drives him to repeat certain patterns after a certain number of years pass, or play a certain role. he may be drawn to fulfil these actions, and the changelings are the only ones who know fate's mechanisms well enough to stop it. or, perhaps, play up on the storyline of the changeling by showing that the mummies have been remembering this prophecy, and bits of it, over the ages. as one of the mummies was called for that purpose, it resonates. perhaps the bad thing happening to her wasnt arcadia, but something else. bringing in the fate mechanics from dancers in the dusk would highlight the themes. perhaps this changeling, like her &quot;keeper&quot;, is true fae? if that is the case, she could have past life memories of her own, alongside the mummies. as for Rome specifically, you can bring in some colorful changeling stuff by playing up on the idea that the seasonal courts may have possibly been born in rome, potentially around the time of the third sothic cycle. it could be possible that the mummies experienced the birth and spread of these courts to the areas outside of rome. playing up on the idea that fate and the fae sometimes chose the same roles to be played by people over time, you could allow the changeling player to take part in those flashbacks as a changeling very much like her from the same keeper. You could even introduce a relic or token that somehow lets the modern changeling remember those events as though she lived them (letting her player keep the xp and not have to act ignorant of the events).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T03:36:25-08:00","id":32266,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas Cleverest. <br /> <br /> I know that what I am doing with the Seasons means that they won't have originated in Rome. However, something important involving them can have occurred there. <br /> <br /> I've made &quot;fate&quot; very abstract in my game. Its a frame of reference and a bit of a crutch for the Mummy's. Though their own understanding of it is quite limited really. For the Changelings all interaction with &quot;fate&quot; takes place through the Wyrd. Which I have presented as something that has an obvious &quot;connection&quot; to fate but the nature of that connection is not really known, but much speculated about among Changelings. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to avoid the &quot;your secretly a true fae&quot; angle. Just because its being played up my the emerging humanity and vulnerability of the Changelings newly exiled Keeper. Likewise, one of the NPC's was this before he became human for a while and then got turned into a Changeling. So I don't want to go back to the same &quot;idea well&quot; if I can help it. <br /> <br /> I was toying with having the Lost Pantheon be a bit deal there. With a sort of &quot;mini-court&quot; of them modeling themselves after the Roman/Greek gods. Also thought about putting something &quot;other&quot; e.g. unique supernatural entity, below the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T07:21:31-08:00","id":32376,"title":"","content":"I like the Lost Pantheon Mini Court idea. I would naturally be inclined to have a High Sekhem encounter between the Mummies and something they can really unload on like a True Fae or a Potent Changeling like a Lost Pantheon God.<br /> <br /> What kind of changeling is the one/s in your group? Contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T05:35:31-08:00","id":33090,"title":"","content":"She's a Fairest Truefriend/Playmate duel kith at Wyrd 5. She's part of the Knights of the Knowledge of the Tongue (which has been great for playing up food related memories). Contract wise she's pretty hefty:<br /> <br /> Fang and Talon 5<br /> Dream 4<br /> Seperation 3<br /> Hearth 3<br /> <br /> Plus a few dream related goblin contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}